  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening the National Response to Trafficking in Persons&#x2019; Prevention, Victim Protection and Prosecution in Burundi</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Burundi):  ..In 2019, to help the GOB make progress on.addressing trafficking in persons (TIP), USAID awarded a grant to the.International Organization for Migration (IOM) to support the &quot;Strengthening.the National Response to Trafficking in Persons&apos; Prevention, Victim Protection,.and Prosecution&quot; activity in Burundi, and another to UNICEF.to implement the &quot;Enhancing the Monitoring of Child&apos;s Rights Violations and.Human Trafficking Victims in Burundi.&quot;  Starting.in 2015 and for six consecutive years, Burundi had been classified as a Tier 3.country under the Trafficking Victims Protection Act of 2000 (TVPA).  In.2021, the TIP report upgraded Burundi to Tier 2 Watchlist, and then in 2022 to.Tier 2.  This improvement in TIP categorization is a result of increased.investigations, prosecutions, and convictions of trafficking crimes, including.by allegedly complicit officials.  For example, the GOB took steps to.increase protections for Burundian migrants abroad, including by establishing.bilateral agreements with key destination countries...FY 2022.funding will continue to support the GOB to sustain and build on gains realized.to date and to focus efforts in areas where the GOB must still meet minimum.standards.  Examples include screening for key indicators of trafficking.among vulnerable populations; providing training to increase awareness among.law enforcement and judicial officials on the 2014 Anti-Trafficking Act and.investigating and prosecuting trafficking cases; and improving GOB oversight of.labor recruitment companies, thereby holding fraudulent labor recruiters.criminally accountable...These.FY 2022 funds satisfy the required $500,000 TIP directive, which is part of.USAID Democracy funds.  ..The.activity is aligned with the BNDP and the Embassy&apos;s ICS Mission Goal 3, Invest.in Society, and the Region: Burundi is a peaceful, open, and stable actor at.home and in the region... .</narrative>
  </description>
